.TH CJSON_SERIALIZE_PRETTY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cjson_serialize_pretty \- serialize a DOM tree to an indented JSON string
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cjson.h>

char *cjson_serialize_pretty(cjson node, unsigned int indent);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Works like cjson_serialize(), but adds newlines and indent spaces for
each nesting level.  An indent of 0 gives the default indent of 4
spaces; use cjson_serialize() for compact output with no indent.  The
members of each object come in the same insertion order as in
cjson_serialize(3).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A null-terminated string on the heap, from the allocator of the root
node.  As with the result of cjson_serialize(3), free it with
cjson_serialize_free() for a tree that uses the default allocator,
and with cjson_serialize_free_mp() for a tree that uses a custom
allocator.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cjson_dictionary_first (3),
.BR cjson_serialize (3)
